.\" The manual page of the Linux packages (NP-091).
.TH KOONAPIN-MCP 1 "October 2026" "Koona Pin" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
koonapin-mcp \- MCP server of Koona Pin for AI assistants
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B koonapin-mcp
.SH DESCRIPTION
An AI assistant on this computer (Claude Code, Cursor and other apps that work with MCP) starts
.B koonapin-mcp
and speaks the Model Context Protocol with it over standard input and output; it is not run by hand.
Each tool call goes to
.BR koonapin (1)
over a socket in
.I $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/koonapin
and the answer comes back. A closed app is started hidden.
.PP
Access is off until it is turned on in Koona Pin: Settings \(-> AI assistants. In
.B Read only
the assistant searches and reads bookmarks, collections and tags; in
.B Read and add
it may also save links to Inbox, tag them, move them to a collection and star them. Nothing is deleted.
.PP
To add it to Claude Code:
.PP
.RS
claude mcp add \-\-scope user koona-pin \-\- /usr/bin/koonapin-mcp
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR koonapin (1),
.BR koonapin-host (1)
